{"author":{"id":"973fc03426eba9a243913e0f6e6823e102397744f60a9ab11c882af948c310c4"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1778938086,"nonce":"a/nj3urhq58QEpqii8T6xoCBjfU=","message":"## Cross-reference: canonical issue/work ledger\n\nCreated `097d2b7` — Mandible canonical issue/work ledger with git-bug import/export.\n\nKey decision captured there: Mandible likely needs to own a central structured issue/work-item ledger rather than treating per-repo `git-bug` refs as the long-term canonical store. Git-Bug import/export should be required from the start because existing issues need migration and compatibility. GitHub Issues support is likely useful later. Other tracker adapters should not be assumed until there is a concrete need.\n\nThe issue also calls out that the Mandible-native path should avoid `git-bug` repo-lock coupling; Git-Bug should become an adapter/sync boundary, not the hot-path dependency for normal issue reads and writes.","files":null}]}